# =============================================================================
# GraphPilot backend environment — copy to backend/.env and edit as needed.
#
# Every variable below has a default in graphpilot/settings.py except
# GRAPHPILOT_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, which the browser UI needs you to set.
#
# GraphPilot makes no provider calls, so there is no API key to configure.
# The MCP server loads backend/.env explicitly, so it is picked up whichever
# directory an MCP client launches the server from.
#
# Put real secrets ONLY in backend/.env (gitignored) — never in this example.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Django core
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Startup refuses to run with DJANGO_DEBUG=false while the key is still one of
# the example values ("django-insecure-dev-only", "replace-with-a-secret-key").
DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=replace-with-a-secret-key
# Truthy values: 1, true, yes.
DJANGO_DEBUG=true
DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend / CORS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API. REQUIRED — settings.py has no
# default, and an empty list blocks the browser editor. `localhost` and
# `127.0.0.1` are distinct origins; list every one you use. Vite is pinned to 5173.
# The launcher (`run.py`) sets this itself for the instance it starts, so this line
# only governs hand-started dev servers.
GRAPHPILOT_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
# Base URL of the React editor, used to build the editUrl that diagram_create returns
# (<base>/editor?diagramPath=<path>).
#
# This is the DEV origin, like everything else in this file. Leaving it here (or empty)
# lets GraphPilot work out at call time which editor is actually running: the dev server
# if one answers on 5173, otherwise the launcher's app. The MCP server is started by your
# IDE and cannot know which of the two you are looking at, so resolving beats guessing.
#
# Change it only to point somewhere neither of those is — a reverse proxy, say. Any value
# other than the dev origin below is treated as a deliberate pin and skips the resolution.
GRAPHPILOT_FRONTEND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagram storage
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A GRAPHPILOT_DEFAULT_WORKSPACE_DIR was offered here and read by nothing: an operator
# who set it got no error and no effect. Every MCP tool takes `workspaceDir` per call,
# which is the design -- a host says which repository it is diagramming, and a default
# would have nothing to default to.
#
# Folder under the workspace holding diagrams/, drafts/ and their SVGs.
GRAPHPILOT_STORAGE_DIR=.graphpilot

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No provider configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GraphPilot makes no LLM calls. The host authors a diagram draft and the backend
# materializes it deterministically, so there is no endpoint, API key, deployment,
# timeout, reasoning effort, projection budget, or review mode to set.
#
# Layout is pinned PyGraphviz 2.0 in-process. No external-dot path, layout
# selector, source-build recovery, or alternate layout algorithm is supported.